Z||000000||Ben84||03-26-2001||09:53 PM||||I recently replaced my alternator, and I'm still having a voltage drain to my 4 cylinder.  During a 30 min. ride in town, my voltage will drop from 13 to 10amps.... Every night, I'll disconnect the neg battery cable to prevent any overnight voltage drain.  What symptoms would you have with  bad fusable links?  Thanks for any Suggestions......||||reg||6
Z||000001||c m west||03-26-2001||09:58 PM||||have you recently added any misc. electrical devices such as an alarm, stereo, fog lights...etc...<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||03-26-2001||11:18 PM||||check the starter||||reg||1
Z||000003||beer_stud_21||03-27-2001||12:25 AM||||I will second indy_resto_guys suggestion and add one of my own.  Definitly check the starter.  I had a hell of a time with voltage drain on my t-bird a while back.  I also changed the alternator which didnt fix the problem.  As it turned out I had both a bad starter and a bad alt (both original one and new [rebuilt] one.  My suggestion would be to check the starter then if that doesnt fix the problem put a hot battery in and put a test light in line with the negitive post of the battery.  If you are getting a short somewhere the light will be on.  Then start by pulling fuses until you get the light to go out.  Good luck and let us know what turns out to be the problem.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ben84||03-27-2001||10:49 PM||||I notice today at a stop signal with the left turn signal...my (rally gage) voltage indicator was moving back and forth (9 to 11), insequence with the turn signal...  I plan on changing my fusable links and have the starter checked.... No new electrical items added lately....<p>[This message has been edited by Ben84 (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||8
